# Bicycles (live canvas)

The P5 bicycle sketch, translated. `wchntMaths` is injected through the
factory (a free name in each `@WCHNTMaths` slot collapses to one factory
argument); every Bicycle keeps the shared reference and pulls `randInt`s in
its helpers.

Construction cannot call `maths.randInt` yet (construction lets only accept
literals/constructions), so the five bikes start from fixed, varied values;
all the ongoing randomness lives in the Bicycle helpers.

`Bicycle::step` builds **one** new Bicycle per tick. Its small helpers return
plain values — `randomY`, `freshSpeed`, `freshSize`, `willTipOver`,
`willDeflate` — instead of rebuilding the whole bike, so the step stays a
single construction.

Drawing lives in WCHNT `## Methods`: `Game::draw` paints the sky and a coarse
field gradient, then asks each bike to draw itself. Target only steps and draws.

## Schema

```
Game = [Bicycle]/bikes Int/w Int/h
Bicycle = Int/x Int/y Int/size Int/dx Int/dy Int/dSize Int/colour @WCHNTMaths/maths
```

## Construction

```
b1 = [:Bicycle 100 320 40 2 0 0 5294335 maths].
b2 = [:Bicycle 300 280 60 1 0 0 16732415 maths].
b3 = [:Bicycle 520 350 30 3 0 0 16752895 maths].
b4 = [:Bicycle 700 300 50 2 0 0 3997695 maths].
b5 = [:Bicycle 160 430 45 1 0 0 13172735 maths].
[:Game [:Array/Bicycle b1 b2 b3 b4 b5] 800 600]
```

## Methods

```
Bicycle::randomY = { Int/h | (h / 2) + maths.randInt((h / 2)) }

Bicycle::freshSpeed = { 1 + maths.randInt(4) }

Bicycle::freshSize = { 50 + maths.randInt(50) }

Bicycle::willTipOver = { maths.randInt(800) == 0 }

Bicycle::willDeflate = { maths.randInt(3000) == 0 }

Bicycle::step = { Int/w, Int/h |
  nx = x + dx.
  wrapped = nx > (w + size).
  rideX = if (wrapped) { (0 - (size * 4)) } else { nx }.
  rideY = if (wrapped) { this.randomY(h) } else { y }.
  landed = (rideY + dy) > (h + 100).
  groundX = if (landed) { -100 } else { rideX }.
  groundY = if (landed) { this.randomY(h) } else { (rideY + dy) }.
  groundDx = if (landed) { this.freshSpeed() } else { dx }.
  groundDy = if (landed) { 0 } else { dy }.
  tipping = this.willTipOver().
  nextDx = if (tipping) { 0 } else { groundDx }.
  nextDy = if (tipping) { 10 } else { groundDy }.
  smaller = size - dSize.
  regrowing = smaller < 1.
  nextX = if (regrowing) { -100 } else { groundX }.
  nextSize = if (regrowing) { this.freshSize() } else { smaller }.
  dSize0 = if (regrowing) { 0 } else { dSize }.
  deflating = this.willDeflate().
  nextDSize = if (deflating) { 1 } else { dSize0 }.
  [:Bicycle nextX groundY nextSize nextDx nextDy nextDSize colour maths]
}

Bicycle::frontWheelX = { x + size + (size / 20) }

Bicycle::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  fx = this.frontWheelX().
  g.beginFill(colour)
   .lineStyle(1, 0x000000)
   .drawCircle(x, y, size / 2)
   .drawCircle(x, y, size / 4)
   .drawCircle(fx, y, size / 2)
   .drawCircle(fx, y, size / 4)
   .drawLine(x, y, fx, y)
   .noStroke()
}

Game::fieldColour = { Int/i, Int/horizon |
  r = 150 - (((i + 1) * horizon) / 100).
  rr = if (r > 0) { r } else { 0 }.
  g = 255 - (((i + 1) * horizon) / 200).
  gg = if (g > 0) { g } else { 0 }.
  b = 100 - (((i + 1) * horizon) / 50).
  bb = if (b > 0) { b } else { 0 }.
  (rr * 65536) + (gg * 256) + bb
}

Game::drawField = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  horizon = h / 2.
  bandH = 8.
  bands = horizon / bandH.
  rows = bands.times({ Int/b |
    y = horizon + (b * bandH).
    g.beginFill(this.fieldColour(b * bandH, horizon)).drawRect(0, y, w, bandH).endFill()
  }).
  g
}

Game::step = {
  moved = bikes.map({ Bicycle/b | b.step(w, h) }).
  [:Game moved w h]
}

Game::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  sky = g.background(0x18EAFF, 0.196).clear().
  field = this.drawField(sky).
  bikes.fold(field, { acc, Bicycle/b | b.draw(acc) })
}
```

## Target

```
%canvas

%requires
WCHNTMaths::randInt(Int) -> Int

%init
var game;

function init() {
    game = GameAssemblage.factory(wchntMaths);
}

%step
function step() {
    game = game.step();
    game.draw(wchntGraphics);
}
```
